INT. CAR DECK - NIGHT FERRY - NIGHT

Rows of parked cars chained to the steel floor. Diesel fumes and cold salt. Overhead lamps sway with the swell.

SORAYA KAMALI (30s, plainclothes agent, wet hair, a pistol held low against her thigh) crouches behind a delivery van. She whispers into her sleeve. Across the aisle, LEV ARKADYEV (50s, silver mustache, cashmere coat) sits calmly on a bumper with a leather case on his knees. He is not hiding.

LEV
You can come out, Agent Kamali. I bought your ticket myself.

She does not move. Behind Lev, MARGUERITE DELACROIX (40s, ship's purser, uniform too crisp) appears at the stairwell door, a keyring in one hand, and stops when she sees the gun. At the far end of the deck, DUTCH PELLEGRINO (60s, deckhand, oil-stained overalls, a wrench) steps out from behind a truck, takes in the three of them, and starts to back away. Soraya stands, aims at Lev, and swings her head toward the noise. Marguerite raises both hands, the keyring jingling. Lev opens the case on his knees and takes out nothing but a thermos.

LEV (CONT'D)
Tea?

SORAYA
Put it down.

LEV
It's tea.

MARGUERITE
(to Soraya)
Miss, I'm only the purser. I was told to bring him the key to the cabin.

SORAYA
Whose cabin?

MARGUERITE
Yours.

Soraya hesitates. Dutch, still backing, bumps a car alarm that begins to whoop. Everyone flinches. Lev does not. He pours tea into the thermos lid, and steam rises in the cold.

LEV
The man you came here to arrest got off at the last port. I wanted to see your face when you understood.

SORAYA
Then why are you still aboard?

LEV
Because you are the one I wanted.

Dutch silences the alarm with a wrench, and the deck goes quiet but for the engines. Marguerite lowers her hands. Soraya lowers the gun an inch, then another. Dutch stays by the truck, wrench loose in his fist, looking at nobody.

DUTCH
(low)
Ma'am, I think the captain knows.

SORAYA
Knows what?

DUTCH
That none of us is going to the next port.

Lev sips his tea. Marguerite looks at her keyring as if she has never seen it before. Soraya raises her gun again, but slower this time, like a woman reading a verdict.

SORAYA
Everyone stay exactly where you are.

LEV
We have nowhere else to be.
